TypeScript allows cross-instance private access. Inside a class, one instance can access a private member on another instance of the same class:

```ts
class A {
  private x = 10;

  sameAs(other: A) {
    return other.x === this.x; // No error
  }
}
```

Java, C#, C++, Swift, and PHP also allow this, while Ruby does not.
